WEBVTT

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.442
One that presumably only had a shower.

00:04:31.466 --> 00:04:33.356
(Music)

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.206
Writers are legendary procrastinators.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.106
The question is why.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.846
And Margaret Atwood has an answer.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.306
MA: I see myself as lazy.

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.045
AG: If you're a procrastinator,

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:47.416
you might have said
the same thing about yourself.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.176
Lazy, slacker, undisciplined.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.033
But is Margaret Atwood,

00:04:53.057 --> 00:04:57.256
bestselling author of
dozens of books, really lazy?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.522
Fuschia Sirois: No, no.

00:04:58.546 --> 00:05:01.061
That's one of the common
myths about procrastination,